[issue-label-exclusions
  [doc [#
scripts/issue_label_exclusions.cxd — the open issues `issue-label-gate` does
not hold to the release label, each by name with its reason (LBL-1, SHIP-2;
#1781). scripts/issue_label_gate.cx reads it.

  [exclude repo=<repository> number=N why='…']
      an open issue that is out of the release by a ruling: in cx-private it
      may lack the release label, in a component repository the release
      title prefix. The reasons are SHIP-2's (ledger/
      rulings_2026_09_30_owner_decision_ship2.md and the audit table
      ledger/issue_audit_2026_09_30_ship2.md).
  [parking milestone=<title> why='…']
      a milestone an open issue may carry: LBL-1 retires the release
      milestone from open issues and keeps v0.19 as a parking milestone for
      what the owner parks by word. Any other milestone on an open issue is
      refused.

A row without a `why=` is refused: the register is evidence, not an excuse.
An exclusion whose issue is closed, or now carries what the gate asks for,
is reported as stale so the row can go.
#]]

  [exclude repo=cx-private number=1697 why='SHIP-2: a duplicate of cx-core-code#2 (the same DEPS_V_DIRS defect, filed in the owning repository)']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=1622 why='SHIP-2: stale and bound by D35a (the five register files moved to their pins)']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=1444 why='SHIP-2: blocked outside the tree — a question for upstream V; posting it is the owner\'s']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=1443 why='owner 2026-10-09: in v0.18 (every V GC/memory/scaling issue) — the V fork half is gaps2\'s; the label is on, this row only records the history']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=1011 why='SHIP-2: blocked outside the tree — needs a Windows runner (parked on v0.19)']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=954 why='SHIP-2: blocked outside the tree — Linguist\'s adoption bar']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=834 why='owner 2026-10-09: in v0.18 (every V GC/memory/scaling issue) — a signal-free linux STW in the V fork, verified on the Linux CI lane; the label is on, this row only records the history']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=801 why='SHIP-2: not scheduled by its own record; its open decision is ruled at scheduling']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=784 why='SHIP-2: not scheduled by its own record — after M5\'s replica consumer']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=521 why='SHIP-2: trigger-bound — multi-node demand proven by a consumer']
  [exclude repo=cx-private number=517 why='SHIP-2: Windows investigation-only by ruling; no Windows host']
  [exclude repo=cx-platform-xap number=9 why='SHIP-2: HKEY-1 (Letter 125 = (a)) puts it after the v0.18.0 cut']  [; version-literal-ok — the ruling names the cut ]
  [exclude repo=cx-platform-xap number=8 why='SHIP-2: a duplicate of cx-platform-xap#4 (the umbrella\'s pre-split path scans)']
  [exclude repo=cx-platform-xap number=6 why='SHIP-2: a duplicate of cx-platform-xap#4 (the same panic of the pinned layout)']

  [parking milestone='v0.19' why='LBL-1: v0.19 stays a parking milestone only for what the owner parks by word']
]
